From bd6c9e8c90fea54369f56bdef9b26bcdea481cfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxolgi <maxolgi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:47:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] avformat: add quicsrt:// protocol (QuicSRT via libquicsrt)

Publish (output) or subscribe (input) to a QuicSRT gateway - SRT over
WebTransport - through libquicsrt's C ABI. Direction decides semantics:
an output publishes ?stream=NAME, an input subscribes to it, so the
same URL works verbatim on both sides.

URL: quicsrt://host:port?stream=NAME[&cert_hash=HEX][&cert_hash_file=PATH][&pki=1][&latency_ms=N]

cert_hash pins the gateway certificate (SHA-256 of the DER, 64 hex
chars) the way browsers pin self-signed WebTransport servers;
cert_hash_file reads the gateway's runtime cert-hash.js and uses its
window.CERT_HASH value ("<hex>" pins, null means PKI); with no cert
parameter the protocol uses normal PKI validation. All parameters are
also protocol AVOptions; a URL parameter takes precedence over the
option value.

MPEG-TS bytes are framed by the library into 188-aligned SRT live
messages of at most 1128 bytes; reads bounce through an internal
one-message buffer; writes loop over the library's partial-accept
contract.

Subscribing retries HTTP 404 and transient transport stalls (live-edge
join); publishing retries a stalled start once. A stalled peer bounds
writes to 30 s and reads to 15 s (the generic rw_timeout overrides
both); the AVIO interrupt callback is honored throughout.

Signed-off-by: maxolgi <maxolgi@users.noreply.github.com>
---
