 @end table
 
+@section quicsrt
+
+QuicSRT - Haivision Secure Reliable Transport over WebTransport - via the
+libquicsrt library. An output publishes the stream name toward the gateway,
+an input subscribes to it, so the same URL works verbatim on both sides.
+The protocol carries MPEG-TS bytes, framed by the library into 188-aligned
+SRT live messages of at most 1128 bytes. Stalled reads and writes fail
+after the generic @option{rw_timeout} when set (defaults: 15 s for a
+dataless read, 30 s for a backpressured write).
+
+The required syntax for a QuicSRT URL is:
+@example
+quicsrt://@var{hostname}:@var{port}[?@var{options}]
+@end example
+
+The following parameters can be set via command line options
+(or in code via @code{AVOption}s):
+
+@table @option
+@item stream=@var{NAME}
+Stream name; required.
+@item cert_hash=@var{HEX}
+SHA-256 of the gateway certificate DER (64 hex chars); pins the
+certificate the way browsers pin self-signed WebTransport gateways.
+@item cert_hash_file=@var{PATH}
+Read the gateway's runtime @file{cert-hash.js} and use its
+@code{window.CERT_HASH} value: a quoted hash pins as @option{cert_hash},
+@code{null} means PKI. A missing or malformed file fails the open.
+@item pki=1
+Normal PKI validation; default when no cert parameter is given.
+@item latency_ms=@var{N}
+TSBPD latency floor. Default is @code{120}.
+@end table
+
 @section zmq
 
 ZeroMQ asynchronous messaging using the libzmq library.
